`EnsureInitialized()` is the only call that starts the part. Every other call returns `Error::NotInitialized`
until it has succeeded, and no read ever starts the part on its own.

## What it does

- Talks to the part through GPIO only: no data bus.
- Power-cycles the part (SHDN_N, when your port drives it) and checks its self-test pulse on OUT.
- Reads OUT several times per reading and reports a floating line instead of a wrong answer.
- Returns `Result<T>` with an `Error` from every call: no exceptions, no heap, no RTTI, no virtual calls.

## Install

```bash
git submodule add https://github.com/kokeb-labs/driver-template.git external/driver-template
```

```cmake
add_subdirectory(external/driver-template)
target_link_libraries(my_app PRIVATE xmpl100::xmpl100)
```

Plain CMake covers any MCU (STM32, RP2040, nRF, ...) and the host.
